<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   What leaves the device when the system backs the app up or transfers it to a new one.

   The app stores nothing of its own: no settings, no library, no history. Everything it
   writes is either a staged conversion under cacheDir, which backup never takes and which
   "Start over" and the staging sweep delete anyway, or WorkManager's queue.

   So WorkManager's queue is the entire payload, and restoring it onto another device is
   wrong rather than merely useless. Every row references a content:// URI granted to this
   install on this device and an output path under this install's cacheDir; the grants do
   not survive the transfer and the cache is not copied, so a restored row names a file that
   cannot exist. ConversionViewModel queries WorkManager by tag on launch to reattach to
   work it did not start, so those rows would not sit inert either: a fresh install would
   come up reattached to a job the user never ran on it. WorkManager declares no backup
   exclusion of its own, so nothing upstream prevents this.

   Excluded from both paths for that reason. allowBackup stays true, because the decision
   belongs here, where it is legible and per-file, rather than as an app-wide switch that
   would also turn off device-to-device transfer for anything this app stores later. A
   contributor who adds real user data should add the include for it here.

   Each file is named rather than the whole "database" domain being excluded in one line.
   A <exclude> carrying no path is skipped unchecked by lint's FullBackupContent detector,
   so that spelling could silently protect nothing; these paths are ones the gate verifies.
   androidx.work.workdb is Room-backed and therefore in WAL mode, hence the two sidecars.

   Note that res/xml/backup_rules.xml is deliberately absent. android:fullBackupContent is
   only read on Android 11 and lower, and minSdk is 33, so it could never have applied here.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" path="androidx.work.workdb" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="androidx.work.workdb-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="androidx.work.workdb-shm" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="androidx.work.util.preferences.xml" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <!-- Same reasoning: a content:// grant does not survive reaching a new device
             either, so a transferred queue is as unusable as a restored one. -->
        <exclude domain="database" path="androidx.work.workdb" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="androidx.work.workdb-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="androidx.work.workdb-shm" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="androidx.work.util.preferences.xml" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
